cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use FlahaX, cite the version used. This checkout prepares unpublished 0.7.0; no new version DOI or release date is assigned. Credit the data sources listed under references."
title: "FlahaX: plant-nutrient chemistry engine for fertilizer formulation and delivery planning"
abstract: >-
  FlahaX turns crop-feed targets, source-water analyses and available products
  into candidate fertilizer and pH-reagent recipes for grower or agronomist
  review. Targets can be supplied directly or designed with Sonneveld's A-D
  sequence and explicit, approved feed corrections from root-zone observations.
  Nutrient fitting and coupled fertilizer/reagent search retain achieved
  concentrations, target residuals, declared limits and bounded-search evidence.
  Rounded dry and separate-stock doses can be checked with declared product,
  dispensing and reagent uncertainty. The software reports calculated pH,
  conductivity estimates and saturation assessments within stated model limits.
  Tank assignments depend on the supplied equipment and compatibility evidence;
  a proposed A/B layout does not certify mixed-stock preparation. TUI, batch and
  Python interfaces preserve units, inputs, source hashes and result identity.
  Numerical chemistry is checked against pinned PHREEQC 3.8.6 references sharing
  thermodynamic data. This is not independent physical validation, a guarantee
  of exact target matching or a global optimum, or operational dosing control.
  Pure Python, with no runtime dependencies.

